-- title:
--   Quadratic base change: unfolded twisted term at a non-scalar class
-- statement:
--   Let $L/K$ be a Galois extension of number fields with $[L:K]=2$, let $\sigma$ be an automorphism of $L$ over $K$ with $\sigma\neq 1$ such that every element of $\mathrm{Gal}(L/K)$ lies in the group generated by $\sigma^{-1}$, and let $D$ be an idele Galois descent datum for $L/K$, i.e. a continuous action of $\mathrm{Gal}(L/K)$ on $\mathbb{A}_L$ by ring automorphisms extending its action on $L$. Fix reals $0<\alpha<\beta$, a constant $c_0\in\mathbb{R}_{\ge 0}$, continuous compactly supported $\varphi:\mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb{A}_L)\to\mathbb{C}$ and $f:\mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb{A}_K)\to\mathbb{C}$. The transfer hypothesis `hcent` assumes: for all $\delta_0\in\mathrm{GL}_2(L)$, $c\in(L\otimes_K\mathbb{A}_K)^\times$ and $u\in\mathbb{A}_K^\times$ such that the norm string $\prod_{i<[L:K]}\sigma^{-i}(\delta)$ of $\delta:=(\delta_0\otimes 1)\cdot c\,I_2$ equals the image of the scalar $u\,I_2$ under $\mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb{A}_K)\to\mathrm{GL}_2(L\otimes_K\mathbb{A}_K)$, and for all Haar measures $\tau$ on the centraliser of $u\,I_2$ in $\mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb{A}_K)$ and $\tau'$ on the $\sigma^{-1}$-twisted centraliser $\{t: t\delta\,\sigma^{-1}(t)^{-1}=\delta\}$, and all $C\in(0,\infty)$: if every right fundamental domain $D'$ for the image of the $\sigma^{-1}$-twisted centraliser of $\delta_0$ in $\mathrm{GL}_2(L)$ inside the twisted centraliser has $\tau'$-measure $C\log(b/a)$ on each slab $\|\det\|_L\in[a,b]$ (determinants taken after transport along $L\otimes_K\mathbb{A}_K\cong\mathbb{A}_L$), and every right fundamental domain for $\mathrm{GL}_2(K)$ inside the centraliser has $\tau$-measure $[L:K]\,C\log(b/a)$ on each slab $\|\det\|_K\in[a,b]$, then any twisted orbital integral $I'$ of $\varphi$ at $\delta$ (for the Haar measure of $\mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb{A}_L)$ pushed to $\mathrm{GL}_2(L\otimes_K\mathbb{A}_K)$, and $\tau'$) equals any orbital integral $I$ of $f$ at $u\,I_2$ (for $c_0\cdot$Haar and $\tau$). Further, $C_H\in(0,\infty)$ is assumed to be the band covolume constant: any subset of a slab $\|\det\|_K\in[a,b]$ which is a fundamental domain for $\mathrm{GL}_2(K)$ acting on that slab has Haar measure $C_H\log(b/a)$. Let $\delta_0\in\mathrm{GL}_2(L)$ and $b_0\in K^\times$ be such that the $\sigma^{-1}$-twisted norm class of $\delta_0$ is the conjugacy class of $b_0 I_2$ in $\mathrm{GL}_2(K)$, and such that $x^{-1}\delta_0\,\sigma^{-1}(x)$ is a scalar matrix for no $x\in\mathrm{GL}_2(L)$. Let $\Psi\subseteq\{g:\|\det g\|_L\in[\alpha,\beta]\}$ be a fundamental domain for the image in $\mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb{A}_L)$ of the $\sigma^{-1}$-twisted centraliser of $\delta_0$ in $\mathrm{GL}_2(L)$, for the adelic Haar measure restricted to that slab, and let $z\in\mathbb{A}_L^\times$. Then $$\int_{\Psi}\varphi\big(x^{-1}\delta_0\,\sigma^{-1}(z\,I_2\cdot x)\big)\,dx=\frac{c_0}{[L:K]}\big(C_H\log(\beta/\alpha)\big)\cdot f\big(N(z)\,b_0\,I_2\big),$$ where $\sigma^{-1}$ acts on $\mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb{A}_L)$ through $D$, $b_0$ is viewed in $\mathbb{A}_K^\times$, $N$ is the idelic norm of the base change $\mathbb{A}_K\to\mathbb{A}_L$, and the real constant (formed from the finite value of $C_H\cdot\log(\beta/\alpha)$) is regarded as a complex number.
--
--   This is the comparison, for a twisted $\sigma$-conjugacy class of the second kind (one not $\sigma$-conjugate to a scalar) whose twisted norm class is central, of the corresponding term of the twisted trace formula for $\mathrm{GL}_2$ over $L$ with the central term of the trace formula over $K$, as in Langlands' quadratic base change for $\mathrm{GL}(2)$. The unfolded integral is evaluated as the band covolume $C_H\log(\beta/\alpha)$ of the rational points in the twisted centraliser times a value of $f$ at a central element; it feeds the variant of this statement formulated directly from the central transfer hypothesis.
